Glide is a native desktop browser. It does not vendor Cloudflare Kitesurf.
It renders pages with the same engine Kitesurf embeds, linked from crates.io
at the versions Kitesurf pins. Those components remain under their own
licenses. Source for each crate is published on crates.io and in the
upstream repositories named below.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Kitesurf
https://github.com/cloudflare/kitesurf
Copyright Cloudflare, Inc.
License: Apache-2.0

Kitesurf is an experimental browser engine that runs on Cloudflare Workers.
Glide follows its stack (Blitz, Stylo, and Vello) rather than linking the
kitesurf-core or renderer-core crates. Those crates are WebAssembly modules
for Workers: their public API is wasm-bindgen, their entropy crates are
configured with the JavaScript backend, and the workspace patches Blitz,
Stylo, Boa, and Vello to paths that Bazel materialises outside the git tree.
See README.md.

Kitesurf itself bundles or patches the projects below. Glide uses the
unpatched crates.io releases of the native subset.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Blitz (blitz, blitz-dom, blitz-html, blitz-paint, blitz-shell, blitz-net,
blitz-traits, stylo_taffy)
https://github.com/DioxusLabs/blitz
Copyright Dioxus Labs and Blitz contributors
License: MIT OR Apache-2.0
Version used by Glide and by Kitesurf: 0.3.0-beta.4

HTML parsing, the DOM, layout (Taffy), and painting.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Stylo (style, selectors, and related Servo crates)
https://github.com/servo/stylo
Copyright Servo contributors
License: Mozilla Public License 2.0
Version pulled in by Blitz 0.3.0-beta.4: 0.22

CSS parsing, cascading, and computed styles. The MPL-2.0 source is the
published crate and the Servo repository above.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
html5ever / markup5ever / xml5ever
https://github.com/servo/html5ever
Copyright Servo contributors
License: MIT OR Apache-2.0

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Vello, Parley, Kurbo, Peniko, and the other Linebender libraries used by
Blitz and anyrender (including vello, vello_cpu, parley, kurbo, peniko,
skrifa, fontations)
https://github.com/linebender/vello
https://github.com/linebender/parley
License: Apache-2.0 OR MIT

Text layout and 2D rendering. Glide's window and `glide --screenshot`
both rasterize with anyrender_vello_cpu (vello_cpu), the CPU renderer
Kitesurf uses on Workers. The window is presented with softbuffer.

